    "description": "Writing is the action to replace a value in a data container with another one. It does not need to be read. The value is simply changed.\n\nWriting happens when a value is being assigned a new value, used with some operators such as ``++`` or ``--``. \n\nThis operation is usually the counterpart of reading. It may also happen at the same time.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    $trunk = 1; // writing 1\n\n    ++$trunk; // reading 1 and writing 2\n\n    echo $trunk; // reading 2\n\n?>",
